n's own files) do not need delegation. Full detail is in the `antigravity` skill. Turn this notice off via the plugin's `coding_policy` option.\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","stdout":"{\r\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\r\n    \"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\",\r\n    \"additionalContext\": \"[antigravity plugin] Routing policy — Claude conducts, Antigravity (agy/Gemini) executes. This is COST-AWARE delegation, NOT \\\"delegate everything\\\".\\n\\nWHEN to delegate to agy:\\n- Bulk / parallel / repetitive work that clearly exceeds the spec + round-trip + verify overhead: mass scaffolding, exhaustive test generation, migrations, long-context reads that return a small digest, fan-out web / Vertex AI Search.\\n- Tools Claude lacks natively: live Google/web search, Vertex AI Search over internal data, Cloud Logging.\\nWHEN NOT to: small, self-contained, or judgement-heavy tasks — do them yourself. Delegating a tiny task is a measured NET LOSS (the round-trip cache_read exceeds the savings).\\n\\nHOW (the cost levers):\\n- Call: \\\"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/scripts/agy-delegate.sh\\\" [--tier flash|flash-lo|pro] [--dir <repo>] [--yolo] \\\"<task>\\\" — or use the antigravity-delegate subagent so file generation happens on Gemini and does not spend Claude tokens.\\n- Keep Claude's context LEAN (biggest lever): take a DIGEST; never re-read the files agy handled or paste its raw output back into the thread.\\n- Pass --dir <repo-root> so agy reads AGENTS.md + the real files instead of pasted context. Batch one big delegation over many small ones. Review the diff, not the whole tree.\\n- Headless (claude -p): delegate SYNCHRONOUSLY — there is no later turn to collect a backgrounded result.\\n\\nVERIFY (non-negotiable): never trust agy's self-reported \\\"GREEN\\\" — actually run the gate yourself in a clean state. agy has been observed altering its own environment (patching installed packages, mock-stubbing deps) to force a pass. Claude owns correctness.\\n\\nSmall one-off edits (including th